#* {{quote-book|en|author=David Michael Smith|chapter=Balsam Fir|title=Stories from the Manger|location=Lincoln, Neb.|publisher=Writers Club Press, {{w|iUniverse}}|year=2001|page=31|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=9FOtBAAAQBAJ&pg=PA31|isbn=978-0-595-19337-0|passage=["]But if I told you the rest of the truth, you wouldn't believe me anyway." / "Try me." / "Guarantee it, you won't," the man teases. "Not in a '''month of Sundays'''."}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Alexandra Morton|authorlink=Alexandra Morton|chapter=3|title=Listening to Whales: What the Orcas Have Taught Us|edition=1st trade paperback|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher={{w|Ballantine Books}}|month=May|year=2002|year_published=June 2004|page=28|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=Rkxk-eifRXwC&pg=PA28|isbn=978-0-345-44288-8|passage=As I listened to the tapes over '''months of Sundays''', it became clear that I would not work with [John] Lilly. I was more interested in the dolphins speaking to dolphins than in the attempts to teach them our language.}}
